ssa, posuere quis aliquet eu\n\nmassa, posuere quis aliquet eu\n\n, facilisis eget urna.\n\nNulla non sagittis ante, eget malesuada velit\n\nVivamus sit amet congue libero\n\n.\n\n.\n\net congue ultrices. Duis purus\n, facilisis eget urna.\n\nNulla non sagittis ante, eget malesuada velit\n\nVivamus sit amet congue libero\n\n.\n\n.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_63606cd0e432", "index": 6, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_a236443a4308", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Monetizatio\n\nn", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_d09e3d468b1b", "index": 7, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_e98b3c079278", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Age of Elemental Chaos\n\nLong ago, the world was ruled by elemental chaos. A young scribe called [PERSON_NAME_29479] figured out how to scribe elemental powers into\n\nsigils. However, he quickly learned about the ramifications of it. He later dedicated his life to neutralizing the powers of the world,\nand eventually created the Archive where he stored all the sigils and taught his order of select few how the balance of the world\nworks.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_3e5a8e3a05f6", "index": 8, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_444747e75f2c", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Archive\n\nThe Scribe created the archive to seal the cards forever and keep the balance of the world.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_630bf5ea802b", "index": 9, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_d09ce16d2f7e", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Rebellion\n\nIn recent years, a group among the Archive disciples decided the main motivation of the Ardal was corrupted by the order elders.\n\nDetermined to put the order to its full potential and power, they called themselves the ?Disciples of Ardal\n\n? and started using the\n\nsigils/cards to dominate the world. They brough back the monsters, and equipped them with sigils of their own.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_badeb17a07f3", "index": 10, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_edb080c0d7a9", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Game Begins\n\u25cf The game begins when the Disciples or\n[PERSON_NAME_29479] make their move for a coup.\n\n\u25cf\n\nThe player enters the scene as an Archive\n\ndisciple where the onboarding funnel\ngoes down and teaches the basics.\n\u25cf After the onboarding, players choose\ntheir starter cards and start with their\nfirst mission to clean out the Temple.\n\n\u25cf\n\nThe player is then sent to the open world\n\nto investigate further.\n\u25cf What they will find out about themselves\nand the legacy of Ardal will surprise\n\nthem.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_f84005f89397", "index": 11, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": []}], "drive_file_id": "f_196bb1ecd0a910067d1a39", "revision_id": "235ddf452e", "created_time": "2025-12-02T15:46:26Z", "modified_time": "2025-12-04T17:52:47Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gslides/data.json", "pointer": "/slides_presentations/77", "field": "presentation_id", "value": "f_7af8adc573c08cc8334651", "record": {"presentation_id": "f_7af8adc573c08cc8334651", "title": "Merge 2D_", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "shared_with_emails": [], "visibility": "private", "pages": [{"object_id": "slide_ff8be6fd8040", "index": 0, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_9ec5a03e13ff", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "MATCH 2D\nITERATION PROPOSITION", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_d0d9e8b07388", "index": 1, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_4d84922af594", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Purpose of the Iteration\n\n\u25cf Trying a new core game innovation that\u2019s easy to develop and test\nfor d1 retention.\n\u25cf Partially making use of the puzzle engine we already have.\n\u25cf To see a match/merge innovation can bring in a fundable d1 metric\nor [USERNAME_6152].", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_7e1db87e4ad8", "index": 2, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_2700e7de0068", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Core Game\n\u25cf\n\nMatch 2 items on the board\nto make a new item.\n\n\u25cf\n\nThe goal is to reach the final\nobject before timer runs out.\n\n\u25cf\n\nMatch the junk items to get rid\nof them.\n\n\u25cf\n\nDifferent boosters.\n\n1.\n\nFreeze Time\n\n2.\n\nMake Match\n\n3.\n\nMix the Board\n\n4.\n\n??\n\nhttps://www.Facebook\n\n.com/\n\n61551040873010/videos/\n\ntrending-merge-game/\n1138554604860646/\n\nhttps://www.YouTube\n\n.com/\n\nshorts/Pgc8BBn3fsw\nhttps://www.YouTube\n\n[USERNAME_60308]\n\n.com/", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_3e5acae20223", "index": 3, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_42e862b15970", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "[USERNAM\nE_29763]\n\nS\n[USERNAME\n_47935]\n\nYou\nwo n\n[USERNA\nME_47604]\n\nh!", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_76d6aa4d7458", "index": 4, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_0291420238ee", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Puzzle Engine Changes\n\n\u25cf\n\nBypass item order can\nbecome the tier list\n\n\u25cf\n\nBypass number can become\nthe tier height.\n\n\u25cf\n\nItems spawn by 2s not threes.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}], "drive_file_id": "f_7af8adc573c08cc8334651", "revision_id": "2f704f2fba", "created_time": "2025-10-15T14:06:55Z", "modified_time": "2025-10-21T12:59:48Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gslides/data.json", "pointer": "/slides_presentations/106", "field": "presentation_id", "value": "f_a56ca06dbec08ebc919adb", "record": {"presentation_id": "f_a56ca06dbec08ebc919adb", "title": "Slack harmonygames", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "shared_with_emails": [], "visibility": "domain", "pages": [{"object_id": "slide_12c0d21dcd16", "index": 0, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_23f929834b10", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Slack\nHarmony\n\nYes, I did come up with a corporate\n\ncorny thing. I?m", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_24230dd6535e", "index": 1, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_c1df3c018e83", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Purpose of This Communication Style\n\u25cf Some people think remote communication is stunting us. (it\u2019s\nrobert, some people are robert)\n\n\u25cf Joking aside, we need to get better at remote communication\ndiscipline with the structure changing and the hard times ahead us.\n?We work\n\nin 3 different time zones.\n\n?Our Slack\n\navailability sucks.\n\n\u25cf We need to establish company communication culture before we go\nthrough another growth phase.\n\u25cf Yes, I\u2019m serious, and yes I will get annoying about it until you get\nused to it. No, I don\u2019t care if you\u2019re the CEO or a lowly intern. The\nrules apply to everyone.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_4bc6801e66ca", "index": 2, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_66fa89647bb3", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "step 1: What?s Your work\n\nHours?", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_41ffe53ba67f", "index": 3, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_3ebb554045b5", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "step 2: Connect Your Calendar To Slack", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_2ef82e240320", "index": 4, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_71c0bfdf1b44", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Step3: Let People Know Your Status", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_b1a0bafe3cfa", "index": 5, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_7ff69682d16f", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Step4: Harmony\n\n\u25cf Coding\n\u25cf Painting\n\u25cf Making Levels\n\nStarter Statuses\n\n\u25cf Lunchbreak\n\u25cf Making Coffee\n\u25cf Painting cat\u2019s nails\n\nBasically,\nwhatever needs\nyour undivided\nattention and\n\nBasically,\nwhatever keeps\nyou away from\n\nchecking a Slack\n\nperiod of time\n\nmessage isn\u2019t\nideal if possible.\n\nwithin you work\n\nSlack\n\nfor a short\n\n\u25cf National Holiday\n\u25cf Personal Day\n\u25cf Sick Day\nBasically,\nwhatever keeps\nyou away from\nSlack\n\nhours.\n\nentire work\n\nfor an\n\nday.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}], "drive_file_id": "f_a56ca06dbec08ebc919adb", "revision_id": "dffa035571", "created_time": "2025-10-27T15:26:56Z", "modified_time": "2025-10-28T16:13:55Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gslides/data.json", "pointer": "/slides_presentations/149", "field": "presentation_id", "value": "f_e37f1de047a1b1e5156607", "record": {"presentation_id": "f_e37f1de047a1b1e5156607", "title": "Mattel _ Harmony Games Barbie_ Dream Life Glow", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "shared_with_emails": [], "visibility": "domain", "pages": [{"object_id": "slide_d6fe356f475f", "index": 0, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_6e76cf0c6f9c", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "A PARTNERSHIP PROPOSAL,\nDec 9 2025\n\nCONFIDENTIAL", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_e486cc3525ff", "index": 1, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_64f8d7e17387", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "We are gamemakers fueled by\nexperience\nKey\nInvestors\n$3M Seed\nin 2023\n\nMatthew Collins\n\n[PERSON_NAME_0174]\n\n[PERSON_NAME_0357]\n\nCo-founder & Game\n[PERSON_NAME_4949]\n\n[PERSON_NAME_6052]\n\n[PERSON_NAME_605\n1]\n\n[PERSON_NAME_0801]\n\nKey Data\n?Founded in 2023\n\n\u25cf ~10 FTEs in core group\n?HQ in the US; A remote\n\nteam with a large hub in\nTurkey, and smaller hubs in\nthe Balkans and South\nAmerica.\n\n[PERSON_NAME_0152]\nCo-founder & CTO", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_5cbacdf6c8b3", "index": 2, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_e2e665fccbf2", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Game Building & Liveops Mastery\n\nGAME MAKERS\n\nCOMPANY BUILDERS\n\n[USERNAME_0451]\n\nOur experience spans\n70+ mobile titles,\nincluding 4X Strategy,\nAction, RPG, and\nCasual games. Our\nefforts have\ncontributed to\ngenerating an\nimpressive $5B+\nrevenue \u2013 showcasing\nour proficiency and\nvalue in the market\n\nWe\u2019ve built and led\nhigh-performing\nteams of\n201000+ organizations.\nWe know how to\ncreate and foster\nremote-first orgs,\ntapping into\nworldwide talent\nwhile keeping\noperational costs in\ncheck.\n\nWe are experts in\nbuilding quests,\nevents, and shop\nsystems for frequent\ncontent updates to\ncreate sense of\nfreshness and a\n\"living world\" at scale\n\nusing ML/AI, pushing\nmonetization and\nretention to new\nheights", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_9191f399c8dd", "index": 3, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_7977df945d3e", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "International Crew with Strong\nPartners to Scale Game Production\n_1504]\n\nLead Game\n\nOLIVER\n\n[PERSON_NAME_150\n5]\n\nMARCUS\n\n[PERSON_NAME_1501]\nSr. Unity\n\nProduct Manager\n\nEngineer\n\n&\n\nSr. VFX Artist\n\nData\n\n[USERNAME_0552]\n\n[PERSON_NA\n\nNDA\nSr. Unity\n\n[PERSON_NA\n\n[USERNAME_0553]\n[PERSON_NAME_1514]\n\nEngineer\n\n_NAME_1509]\n\n[PERSON_NAME_1516]\n\n[USERNAME_1051]\n\n[USERNAME_1052]\n\nK\n\nGAME STUDIO\n\n[PERSON_N\nAME_0470]\n\n(Engineering Partner\n\nSTUDIO\n(Domino Delights\n\nto\n\nscale internal team up to\n8+ Engineers)\n)", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_e3797b57680c", "index": 4, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_50b8af266d77", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Vision\nBuild the world\u2019s best puzzle RPGs\n\nMission\nRapidly build and test breakthrough game\nmechanics, then scale them with\nHarmony\n\n?s AI engine", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_d591ac346d2e", "index": 5, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_5bbc30435c5e", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Dream Life\n[USERNAM\nE_41778]\n\nA living, evolving\nBarbie Land\n\nfor Barbie\n\ngirls of all ages where we\ncelebrate the timeless\nmessage:\nYou can be anything!", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_b29eacc03428", "index": 6, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_6d6fbf67374b", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Welcome to Barbie\n\nLand\ntakes place in\n\nBarbie Dream Glow\n\nan online Barbie Land\n\nthat the\n\nplayer has to build from the ground\nup.\nwith full\ndecoration and customization\noptions.\nThe Dreamhouse\n\nBarbie\n\n?s iconic friends\n\nas\n\nneighbours players can visit and\n\ninteract with.\nVendors like fashion houses, hair\nsalons, bakeries, and more.\n\nsocial\n\nhubs\n\nlike parks, the beach,\n\npicnic areas, and more.\n\nEach spot unlocks at different\nprogress points and comes with its\nown unique storyline.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_89ffefa4e47c", "index": 7, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_a3bfb4b7315e", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Dream Life Glow:\nMarket Opportunity\nGlobal mobile life sim / fashion / idle sim games\n\n\u2605\n\nRoughly $2B in annual player spend across\nlife simulation, fashion, dress up, and idle\nsim titles on mobile.\n\nBarbie\n\n\u2605\n\ncompatible audience on mobile\n\n150\u2013250M global players who already\nengage\n\nwith dollhouse, dress up, home\n\ndesign, cozy, and lifestyle games.\n\u2605\n\nProven\n\nreach: Barbie Dreamhouse\n\nAdventures\n\nalone has 100M+ downloads\n\nwith lighter systems and monetization.\nTarget for Barbie\n\n\u2605\n\n\u2605\n\n: Dream Life Glow\n\nRealistic target: 100M dollars lifetime\nrevenue if the game lands in the upper tier\nof life sim / idle charts.\nUpside: multi hundred million dollar\npotential with strong live ops, cross\npromotion, and alignment with Barbie\n\nproduct launches.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_32a056224070", "index": 8, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_f06069d032b2", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Why It Works?\nSimulation is a\naudience fit.\n\nProven\n\nIdle Simulation is the best complimentary genre to simulation for\nthe Barbie\n\naudience.\n\n\u2605 Allows for complex progression systems that opens up\ndeep engagement\n\nand monetization\n\n\u2605 Easy to learn\n\u2605 Tangible and meaningful progression\n\u2605 Broad audience\n\u2605 Balanced monetization\n\u2605 Diverse World Building", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_042a5359cdd3", "index": 9, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_02accc7bc1bf", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Example Gameplay Flow\n\nPlayer chooses\nmedicine\n\nCheck in the\npatient\n\nExamine the\npatient\n\nCheck out the\npatient", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_1fb11902c30e", "index": 10, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_f6b854d9e743", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Example Progression Flow\n\nUpgrade and\ndecorate the space\n\nHire staff\n\nEach choice has\ndifferent perks\n\nFurther your career as\nyou", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_71f1dfba8a65", "index": 11, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_9b7a8554a077", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Progression\n\nmeta\nAfter completing the story via core gameplay, each building reveals a meta\n\nprogression\n\nelement.\n\nUnlock a minigame for every Barbie Friend\n\nUnlock vendors in the Barbie\n\nstoryline you finish!\n\nthe story and get special menu items and discounts.\n\nLand through finishing", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_e91cf9cc52ae", "index": 12, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_86307615feba", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Live Operations Via Narrative\nDesigned for long term retention and higher LTV\n\nTraditionally, live operations are\npresented via dual columns on either\nside of the main menu.\nBarbie Dream Glow\n\nis designed to\n\ntake live operations to the next level.\nInstead of repetitive liveops event,\neach liveops event occurs during\nrandom times, and has a narrative tie\nto the core gameplay.\nThis ensures smart Push\n\nnotification\n\nusage, and incentive to log into the\ngame to check out what\u2019s happening\nin the ever alive Barbie\n\nland for better\n\nretention and gameplay metrics.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_b538925f857b", "index": 13, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_92fedd242572", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Smart Product Placement via\nLiveOps\nCurated Barbie\n\nproducts can be\nintroduced in the\ngame via a live\noperations event.\nThis way, players\nenjoy fresh content\nfrequently and There\n\nis\n\nalways something new\nto do in the Barbie\n\nLand that brings time\nlimited accessories\nand skins for their\nBarbie\n\npersonas.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_a3655b7bba1d", "index": 14, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_f09e1df55447", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "A Partnership in Global Entertainment\n\n\u25cf\n\nbrands like Barbie\n\n\u25cf\n\niconic\n\nGlobal family entertainment leader :\n\n, Hot Wheels, UNO, and more.\n\nmedia worlds.\n\nstories that feel personal and lasting.\n\u25cf\n\nethical, positive marketing and strong fan\n\nin kids and family marketing, licensing, and\n\u25cf\n\nEvergreen product roadmap: constant flow of\n\ncommunities.\n\n\u25cf\n\nScalability and liveops: Proven\n\ncontent\n\npipeline, events, segmentation, and A/B\n\nnew dolls, playsets, and content that can plug\ndirectly into live games.\n\nAuthentic worlds and communities: design\nexperiences that extend beyond the game with\n\nBrand and retail powerhouse: deep expertise\nglobal distribution.\n\nPlayer centered mission: care deeply about\nplayers and build heartfelt games and untold\n\nFranchise and IP builder: decades of\nstorytelling, character development, and cross-\n\n\u25cf\n\n\u25cf\n\ndiscipline.\n\u25cf\n\nExecution speed: small and cost-efficient\nteam, short loops, weekly ship cadence.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_0e2db241bf6d", "index": 15, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_650670700e2d", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Thanks For Your Attention!", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}], "drive_file_id": "f_e37f1de047a1b1e5156607", "revision_id": "b7b3689d5e", "created_time": "2025-11-12T07:10:29Z", "modified_time": "2025-12-09T16:54:29Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gslides/data.json", "pointer": "/slides_presentations/151", "field": "presentation_id", "value": "f_e5d882de8e80f1ea5839cc", "record": {"presentation_id": "f_e5d882de8e80f1ea5839cc", "title": "Vanilla Match 3D", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "shared_with_emails": ["claire.morgan@harmonygames.co", "robert@harmonygames.co", "vincent.parker@harmonygames.co", "marcus.bennett@harmonygames.co", "leonard.hayes@harmonygames.co", "arthur.blake@harmonygames.co", "brian.foster@harmonygames.co", "douglas@harmonygames.co", "calvin.price@harmonygames.co", "owen.baker@harmonygames.co", "oliver.brooks@harmonygames.co"], "visibility": "domain", "pages": [{"object_id": "slide_660a6e87faf2", "index": 0, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_aae8f277f3a9", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "VANILLA MATCH 3D\nITERATION PROPOSITION", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_79d43c151b99", "index": 1, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_0de7c3175d97", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Purpose of the Iteration\n\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nCreating an iteration that makes use of most of the elements built with minimum changes.\nMaking full use of the puzzle engine we built.\nTesting the full potential of the core game without innovative RPG elements in terms of\nretaining metrics and LTV.\n#lite", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_6cef5a88ef5d", "index": 2, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_83058c71acea", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "In-Level Core Game Changes\n\u25cf\n\nNo more zombies :(\n\n\u25cf\n\nCore game takes up the\nwhole screen.\n\n\u25cf\n\nPlatform moves down\n\n\u25cf\n\nThere\n\nare now\n\n\u25cf\n\nThere\n\nis a timer.\n\nobjectives.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_e7f3adb623b8", "index": 3, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_a3c2c04690d0", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "meta\n\n-Game Changes\nCard mechanic\n\nis removed\n\ncompletely to be iterated later\n\u25cf\n\nComing Soon text on the icon\n\n\u25cf\n\nDisable cards from backend,\nshop, Zombie lane, and\n\nrewards.\n\nComing\nsoon", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_cdf45f3b37ac", "index": 4, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_756788416bf3", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Puzzle Engine Changes\n\n\u25cf\n\nNumber of bypass items\nbecome number of objective\ncontainers.\n\n\u25cf\n\nIf an object is marked bypass,\ntheir sprite becomes in the\nimage in the container", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_798bf04012ea", "index": 5, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_07e23e813647", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Questions to Consider\n\u274f What do we do with the backend, assuming the economy will be\ndifferent?\ncost.)\n\u274f Do we publish it as a new game? (no, and if yes consider DOUGLAS\n\u274f Time to make a hoover booster? (quick)\n\u274f How hard is to disable cards from the game? (no problems)\nwill be 8-10 new\n\u274f How hard is it to update the quest list assuming There\nquests that will be moderately time consuming?\n\u274f Can we easily have RV for the iteration? (yes)\n\u274f What is removing the split screen will do the game modes? Can we keep\nthem easily? (little bit complicated)\n\u274f Overall time and engineering resource assessment? (2-3 a month or so)\nI missed?\n\u274f Any invisible work", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_3d795e04198d", "index": 6, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_b5356b833516", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Essential Art Needs (day or two)\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nNew gray background\nNew UI for the timer, level display\nIsland, and objective container.\n\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nNew store screenshots\nNew creatives\nA few loading/infographic screens\nthat have tips about the gameplay\n\n\u25cf\n\nAny invisible work\n\nI missed?\n\nNice-to-Have (2-3 weeks)\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nColor iteration to go with the dark gray\nbackground. (already done)\nNew event icon polishes (I\u2019ll generate)\nRemoval of zombie theme from UI assuming\nreplacement will be generic.\nSimple splash screen and home screen that\ndoesn\u2019t have zombies.\nA CPI-friendly mascot\n\nComing\nsoon", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_29947ef8f29c", "index": 7, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": []}], "drive_file_id": "f_e5d882de8e80f1ea5839cc", "revision_id": "c3a5447698", "created_time": "2025-10-15T12:38:43Z", "modified_time": "2025-10-21T20:52:05Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gslides/data.json", "pointer": "/slides_presentations/163", "field": "presentation_id", "value": "f_ffd7fdb72db51775ff6d67", "record": {"presentation_id": "f_ffd7fdb72db51775ff6d67", "title": "ZM Level Design Guide", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "shared_with_emails": [], "visibility": "domain", "pages": [{"object_id": "slide_8124cbdb6d57", "index": 0, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_eea47285eb31", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "\u25cf\n\ncore design principles are shown on\n\n\u25cf\n\nThe first 100 levels are to teach the player\nall the core gameplay values and strategies\nthey can form.\nMake levels that either rewards mastery or\nspeed. Make sure to rotate between them\nsufficiently for gameplay variety.\nMonochromatic and texture heavy levels\nshould reward speed, whereas levels where\neither an item or zombie is being introduced\nshould reward mastery instead should be a\n\u201cno brainer\u201d level.\nThe approaches can be combined after level\n100.\n\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\n\u25cf\n\u2756\n\u2756\n\u2756\n\u25cf\n\nDon\u2019t match approaches back to back too\nmuch.\nDon\u2019t match more than 2 until level 200\nMatch 3 sparingly after level 200.\nThe levels solution should be obvious in the\nfirst glance. That\u2019s not to say levels should\nbe easy, it just means, on the first look, the\nstrategy should be obvious, especially for\nthe first 100 levels. We\u2019ll confuse players\nlater on after d7 levels by introducing nonobvious levels or trick strategy levels so in\nearly levels, please avoid these kind of\ntricks.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_9b1cbc1302b7", "index": 1, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_cae3c86f2506", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "How To Use\nColors?\n\nWe have 4 types of color levels. Levels should try to\nadhere to these types or use lighter monster track if\nusing a combination of multiple.\n\nMonochrome\n\u25cf\n\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nWhen making monochrome levels, use objects of the same color that has\nat least one other color or detail that\u2019s in another color. Pure color items\nare okay, but they shouldn\u2019t exceed 2-3 and should be still visually\ndistinguishable via shape or texture.\nUse monochrome levels sparingly and make sure to rotate between colors.\nWhen making monochromatic levels make sure you choose a middle\nsaturation unless some textures make it okay to go higher or lower.\nPlayers take a longer time to solve a monochrome level so make sure to\ncompensate with a more forgiving monster track.\nTry to follow with a more forgiving level after a monochromatic level. Aim\nto follow up with a level that has items distinguishable through shape and\ntexture (e.g. like a ball level). At the very least, try to change up the\ngameplay style focus.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_505edb1b6cd5", "index": 2, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_fa294b1790df", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Complementary Color\nUsage\n\u25cf\n\nWhen players look at a level made out of complementary colors, they will perceive it as a\nwhole. Use this to to the levels advantage to steer players towards a certain color via texture\n\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\n\u25cf\n\nand saturation.\nThis type of level will get hard in the middle. So make sure your monster track intensifies or\ndecrease monster track difficulty based on the level difficulty you want. Levels after 70ish are\neligible to support an increase in the middle rhythm in a complementary color level.\nDistribution of colors doesn\u2019t really matter. If you have equal amount of the colors, player will\ngravitate towards texture and saturation. Same is true if one color is less dominant, therefore\nlooking more prominent on top of it\u2019s complementary counterpart. Use forced tops and\nbottoms if you are concerned about preventing abuse.\nGood practice is to use items and details of various sizes for each color. Otherwise the level\nwill be unfairly difficult and luck will play too much role. If your goal is to create more rhythm\ntowards the end, you can use similar items but I recommend you force them bottom to create\na nice gameplay shift and layer\n\n.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_8974b3d14811", "index": 3, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_2f2e52263d2c", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Analogue\nLevels\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nAnalogue levels are a great alternative to monochrome levels and allow for more flexibility in\nitem selection.\nAnalogue levels items should be more or less split equally between colors. If There\n\nis an\n\nimbalance, unlike the complimentary levels, the level will always be a lot more easier.\nAnalogue levels are great for using the same item of different colors.\nIf you go for three analogue colors, the third color, either the left one or the right one needs\nto become an accent color and have less objects in that color. If you want accent items\nwithout adding another color, go for texture accents.\nNeutral colors can always be used as an alternative to a third analogue.\n\nTexture\naccent\n\nExample of third\nanalogue being an\naccent", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_486accbd66a2", "index": 4, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_44fedd1ec3f5", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Triad and Tetrad\nLevels\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nTriad and Tetrad levels should be considered when a noisy level is required for variety.\nThey can use any triad and tetrad combination and include a neutral, but sparingly.\nNeutrals shouldn\u2019t include items the same color as the triad or the tetrad. So if a red shuriken\nis present, a gray shuriken shouldn\u2019t be in the level. So it should be avoided in general, but\nokay to use sparingly.\nMake sure to use textures in such levels.\nUse these levels if you want to create levels with similar size items.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_3c9f9f518693", "index": 5, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_27c517cb08cd", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Experimental\nLevels\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nHere is an example of an experimental level. It combines a monochrome level with a texture\nchallenge.\nFeel free to throw this kind of level in the funnel to see player reaction for readiness for\nmechanic combination etc.\nIf you have this type of experimental level, make sure it falls in the middle of well learned\npassive skills. For example make a level like this after introducing monochromatic levels and\ntexture challenge levels and There\n\nmuscle in both mechanics.\n\nare enough of them for the players to have gained the", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_f8ebde712a7e", "index": 6, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_3390890778fa", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "The Role of Rhythm in Level Making\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nA good level should have a rhythm unique to that level. And a good curve should include variety of level rhythms.\nFor casual games, avoid using rhythm curves that start fast and slow down over time. Unless you catch a fun one, start slow\nand build into it.\nThe core principle of using rhythm in level making is to make sure the player falls into repetitive motion and gets zoned\nout/relaxed while engaging with the content. So as long as this is achieved, your rhythm is working.\nSince we\u2019re working with CPM, you can easily test your methods with the level design bot.\nYou can use rhythm via objects or the monsters, both will work\n\n.\n\nItem Rhythm\n\n\u25cf\n\nA good level should have a rhythm unique to that\nlevel. And a good curve should include variety of\nlevel rhythms.\n\nMonster Rhythm\n\u25cf\n\nA good level should have a rhythm unique to that\nlevel. And a good curve should include variety of\nlevel rhythms.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_3ce9bbf32d1c", "index": 7, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_0f581d17d269", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "Core Progression Principles\n\u25cf\n\nThe main principle of the level progression is subjecting players to a certain CPM, and failing\nthem if they don\u2019t match the speed required.\nThis requirement begins at very low CPMs until the core game learning curve levels are passed and then\nprogressively becomes harder, capping at a CPM that will be determined by the data later but projected\nto land at 100-120 CPM as a plateau.\nAs a secondary target, the level durations should also curve and increase over time, eventually reaching\nthe cap of 90-120 seconds based on the objects of a level.\n\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nOther Considerations\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\u25cf\n\nThe levels should have zombies reaching the cannon at the target CPM. The logic being, if the players\n\nfalls short of the CPM the zombies would pile at the cannon and create urgency.\nTry to put zombies at exact times to make sure to achieve this effect, especially in levels that have area\naffect items to ensure easier balance.\nLevel balance target is for players to finish a level without cards, winstreaks, or boosters at\nthe target CPM.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}, {"object_id": "slide_a693a1d83078", "index": 8, "layout": "BLANK", "elements": [{"object_id": "el_cdb9214a15f4", "kind": "TEXT_BOX", "text": "CPM Targets\n1-30 \u2192 50 CPM\n30-75 \u2192 60CPM\n75-100 ? 70 CPM\n\n100-150 \u2192 75 CPM (will change according to data) = Almost 2 minutes to clear 48 items\n150 - onward \u2192 80-90 CPM (will change according to data)\n\nDuration\nTargets\n\nLevels 1-5 \u2192 15 seconds\nLevels 5-10 \u2192 25 seconds\nLevels 10-15 \u2192 35 seconds\nLevels 25-40 \u2192 45 seconds\nLevels 40-75 \u2192 60 seconds\nLevels 75-100 \u2192 75 seconds\nLevels 100-150 \u2192 90 seconds\nLevels 150-onward \u2192 90-120 seconds.\n\nItem Targets\n3 color scheme max\n\nwith occasional\n\nmulticolor levels or 4 for item intro\nlevels.\n4-5 quantity (6 max)\n5-6 unique items (6 max)\nAfter level 150 we\u2019ll bump this by\n1, and CPM by 5 until the\nretention data endures the\nincreased difficulty.", "placeholder_type": null, "x_emu": 0, "y_emu": 0, "width_emu": 9144000, "height_emu": 5143500}]}], "drive_file_id": "f_ffd7fdb72db51775ff6d67", "revision_id": "fbf725fb03", "created_time": "2025-09-09T14:37:31Z", "modified_time": "2025-09-11T17:04:12Z"}}], "records_checked": 164, "files_selected": 1, "files_completed": 1, "scan_complete": true, "errors": []}}, "files_read_this_call": 3, "sources": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gslides/data.json", "manifest_sha256": "c3782541395e178187d732eb429a7e69926244856147a8c4f5091b0f9e7a7426", "freshness": "f234fec647af2dbc77f101b0eb50bf1c0f7ba155b2b960031fe8340010fbbb1f"}], "scan_complete": true, "persona_filtered": false, "backend": "grouped-record-scan", "scope_note": "Exact direct fields in selected arrays. No SQL is applied. Absence/uniqueness is supported only within complete declared scopes. Manifest hashes are declared provenance, not fresh full-content hashes."}, "checksum": "baab025f6cdf01c6ccabb4806d8d4362e47ca01dd6baf05b8449c3f07004104d"}